The six ESCHA_MM eval cases were nested inside the ssm_conv d_conv/d_inner loops and
therefore registered 9x each (that is the "54/54"). Moved them out.

Added eval cases at ncols 205 (ESCHA2) and 133 (ESCHA3). Every prior eval case had
ncols <= 4, so the incoming Vulkan column-chunk guard (32 columns/dispatch) would run a
single iteration with col_offset == 0 and be tested vacuously. These two cross six/four
chunk boundaries and leave ragged tails.

Added a perf sweep over ncols {1,8,64,256,512,1024,2048} on the real 27B projection
shapes to measure per-dispatch duration directly. HAZARD (F-124): running that sweep
before the column-chunk guard exists walks into the exact shape that froze the host
twice. Do not run perf -o ESCHA_MM until the guard lands.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: none yet (test registration only); unlocks the ncols duration curve
Lane: lane-164
---
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp b/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
index 41a1192a3..8ff2b11c0 100644
